   "createdAt": "2026-07-22T16:03:18.000Z",
   "likeCount": 4810,
   "commentCount": 182,
   "isAvailable": true,
   "caption": "Probiotic Mango Soda — using just the pits, peels, and water!\n\nYou can create a super healthy, refreshing, naturally bubbly soda with things most people would throw into the trash can! So yes, this is a free product to make and it’s super beneficial for you too. And, it’s also the most delicious thing ever!\n\nI fermented mango peels, mango pits, in water for 6 days. Next I strained it and added in some coconut sugar. The coconut sugar is there solely to feed the yeast and produce CO2 during the second ferment. I bottle the mango soda with the sugar in airtight bottles and allow to further ferment until super bubbly, then I move the sodas to the fridge!\n\nYou can do this with most any fruit! Ill be posting a more detailed how-to on my site in the coming days, so stay tuned. But until then let me know if you have any questions!",
